For integrating with business softwares like civil status and town planning, we can utilize our experience with ERP/CRM connectors for systems like SAP, Salesforce, Oracle, Ciril/ARPÈGE, and OXALIS. We also have knowledge of Ged systems such as Alfresco, Maarch Courrier, and OpenKM, which can be useful for integrating with electronic management of documents (EDM).

To integrate with user directories, we can use our experience with identity providers like Active Directory/LDAP, Keycloak, and FranceConnect.

In terms of architecture, I propose a microservices-based approach with containerization using Docker and orchestration using Kubernetes (K8s) and Helm. This will enable us to deploy and manage the integrated system efficiently and ensure high performance.

We can use our experience with message brokers like Apache Kafka and RabbitMQ to handle communication between different microservices and systems. Additionally, our expertise in monitoring tools like Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK stack will help us ensure the system's availability and performance meet the client's expectations.

To guarantee high availability, we can design the system to be deployed on a cloud provider with which we have experience, such as OVHcloud, Scaleway, or Outscale (SecNumCloud), and utilize their scalability features. Our experience with Terraform and Ansible as IaC tools will also help us manage the infrastructure efficiently.

Overall, our current technology stack can meet the client's integration requirements, and a well-designed microservices-based architecture can ensure seamless integration and high performance.
