2026-05-26 11:03:36,209 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent received: The tender emphasizes strict GDPR compliance, data sovereignty, and explicability of AI recommendations. How can we ensure that our solution meets these regulatory requirements, and what security controls should be implemented to protect sensitive data?
2026-05-26 11:04:55,452 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-05-26 11:04:55,452 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: As the Security and Compliance Officer at Nexus Engineering S.r.l., I can confirm that our company has experience with regulatory frameworks such as GDPR and has appointed a Data Protection Officer (DPO) whose contact is dpo@nexus-engineering.it. We are also certified with ISO 27001, which includes the scope of Design, development, and operation of AI-powered information systems.

To ensure strict GDPR compliance, we can implement data anonymization tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) or custom NER models to protect sensitive data. Our company has experience with anonymisation tools and can ensure that personal data is not used in training pipelines without proper anonymization. We also have a cross-border transfer policy that prohibits transfers by default unless there's an explicit legal basis.

For data sovereignty, we can ensure that all data is hosted exclusively within the European Union (EU), as per our standard data residency policy. This aligns with the client's requirement for data sovereignty.

Regarding explicability of AI recommendations, our company has experience with AI security controls such as output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, and confidence threshold escalation. We can also provide model isolation through an inference API to prevent direct access to models by end-users. Additionally, we conduct regular security reviews of model updates to ensure the integrity of our AI solutions.

To protect sensitive data, we should implement robust security controls such as multi-factor authentication (MFA) using TOTP or hardware tokens (FIDO2), role-based access control (RBAC), and privileged access management (PAM) solutions like CyberArk Conjur or HashiCorp Vault. We also have experience with zero-trust architecture, micro-segmentation, and defense-in-depth patterns to protect against unauthorized access.

Our incident response plan includes a Security Incident Response Team (SIRT) and playbooks for responding to security incidents, ensuring that we can quickly respond to any potential data breaches or security incidents. Our average time to conduct a Data Protection Impact Assessment (DPIA) is 3 weeks, which can help identify and mitigate potential risks associated with our AI solution.

By implementing these measures, we can ensure that our solution meets the client's regulatory requirements for GDPR compliance, data sovereignty, and explicability of AI recommendations while protecting sensitive data.
